@startuml storage-diagnostics
title M5: committed result and diagnostic publication
participant "Host / IPC" as Host
participant "Core Engine" as Engine
participant "Runner" as Runner
database "SQLite result store" as Store
participant "Host JSONL log" as Log
Host -> Engine : Start / StartAuto
Engine --> Host : admission (RunId / AutoId)
Engine -> Log : RunStarted / StageEntered (outside gate)
Engine -> Runner : execute admitted run
Runner -> Runner : Prepare / Acquire / Inspect
Runner -> Engine : enter persistence under gate
Engine --> Runner : Persisting
Runner -> Store : INSERT in transaction
alt commit succeeds
Store --> Runner : persisted result
Runner --> Engine : inspection result
else constraint / busy failure
Store --> Runner : exception / rollback
Runner --> Engine : error with ComputedResult
end
Engine -> Engine : finish callbacks and timer / decide stable outcome
Engine -> Log : RunCompleted with IDs and cause (outside gate)
Log --> Engine : recorded or write failure isolated
Engine -> Engine : publish snapshot / release slot / complete handle
Host -> Store : GetResult / SearchResults
Store --> Host : committed rows only
note over Store : committed rows survive Host restart
Host -> Engine : await DisposeAsync
Engine --> Host : work and diagnostic calls finished
Host -> Log : close after adapters and IPC stop
@enduml
